This eliminates re-derivation drift in the trainer and improves reproducibility and downstream ARI.

- Record and expose a canonical standardize_symbol routine in preprocess_metadata (string description and examples) and add a checksum of the standardized var_names. This lets training code verify exact symbol canonicalization and prevents subtle misalignments that hurt pathway signals.

- Strengthen split stratification. Keep the current dataset||protocol stratification but enforce minimum counts per group for val/test when n≥3 (e.g., at least one sample per non-singleton group) and log any groups falling below the minimum. This avoids empty-batch validation/test artifacts that can bias early stopping and ARI.

- Add optional covariate: log library size. Store obs['log_library_size'] = log1p(nCount_RNA) and, if desired, append it to obsm['covariates'] (config-gated). This can reduce residual library-size effects in the encoder, sharpening clusters.

- Store counts as compact integers. Cast layers['counts'] to int32 CSR before writing to reduce disk/memory and ensure integer Poisson/NB consistency downstream; keep X as float32 log1p CPM.

- Enforce deterministic dummy encoding. Save the category order for domain/protocol/dataset in preprocess_metadata and ensure get_dummies uses that order to prevent covariate column drift across runs (further stabilizing z and clustering).</FEEDBACK>


