nt scale in W_prior initialization and stabilizes group sparsity across heterogeneous set sizes.\n- Leverage meta_info to prune low-value genes from sets: if summary_type or summary_name indicate non-coding categories with low expression in scRNA-seq (e.g., many lincRNAs/pseudogenes), filter them from sets unless present and expressed in the dataset (use a minimal nonzero-count threshold). This reduces noise, especially in marker aggregations.\n- Improve marker aggregation quality by evidence- or tissue-aware filtering: use marker_source/PMID/tissue_class in Cell_marker_Human.xlsx to keep immune/blood-relevant markers and require minimal evidence (e.g., ≥2 sources or PMIDs) before inclusion. This increases precision for PBMC-like data and improves ARI.\n- De-duplicate sets within-source first and only then across sources, and compute Jaccard after removing ubiquitous “housekeeping” genes (e.g., ribosomal/mitochondrial and the most frequent 1–2% of genes by membership). This preserves complementary information while removing truly redundant sets.\n- Ensure CSR structures are canonicalized (sort_indices, eliminate_zeros) before saving membership/graphs to avoid downstream sparse ops overhead and surprises at load time."}</FEEDBACK>

