<LM_OUTPUT> {"role": "model", "feedback": "- Fix Laplacian regularizer (currently no gradients): laplacian_smoothness() detaches Wp, so the penalty doesn’t train W_prior. Precompute L_sub as torch sparse COO and compute w^T L w in torch without detach, e.g. build L_coo = torch.sparse_coo_tensor(...), then LW = torch.sparse.mm(L_coo, Wp_masked) and return torch.sum(Wp_masked * LW).\n- AMP + grad clipping: call scaler.unscale_(opt) before nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_ to ensure proper clipping under autocast.\n- Numerics in NB loss under AMP: compute lgamma/log terms in fp32 by disabling autocast inside nb_nll (with torch.cuda.amp.autocast(enabled=False)) and casting y, mu, theta to float32.\n- Unify gene symbol standardization between preprocess and model: reuse the exact standardize_symbol from preprocessing (uppercase + drop dot-suffix) to prevent silent gene misalignment. Better: skip re-deriving alignment in model and load preprocess_metadata.json to get prior_gene_indices_in_order, model_gene_indices, and kept_set_indices; subset prior matrices accordingly for perfect reproducibility.\n- Respect prior set selection from preprocessing: don’t re-trim sets in align_genes_to_prior; instead subset membership to kept_set_indices from preprocess. Map prior_set_weights by a stable key (set_id if present) to the filtered set order; fall back to a constant λ0 if missing.\n- Decoder link: softmax over genes + NB is a mismatch with the independent NB assumption. Switch to a softplus rate with library-size offset (e.g., mu = softplus(logits) * size_factor) or log-link (log mu = logits + log size_factor). Keep W_prior masking unchanged.\n- Enforce non-negativity on W_prior: parameterize W_prior_raw and use Wp = softplus(W_prior_raw) * mask so prior-aligned contributions remain interpretable and don’t cancel with W_free.\n- Optimizer parameter groups: remove weight decay from biases and dispersion (bias_gene, bias_dataset, theta_unconstrained) to avoid shrinking nuisance terms; optionally lower decay on W_prior relative to W_free.\n- MMD on z_free is effectively zero across epochs; ensure mixed batches: use a balanced batch sampler per dataset so each minibatch contains ≥2 cells per dataset; consider stronger multi-kernel MMD or CORAL if still ineffective.\n- Save full latent outputs and priors for downstream: write z_prior, z_free to obsm for all cells; persist masked W_prior, W_free, b_g, theta_g as .npy/.npz and record the set/genes order used.\n- Minor: use preprocess splits for neighbor graph/Leiden bootstrap stability (resampling cells) as planned; log chosen resolution and modularity; add monitoring of mean|z_prior| sparsity to logs (already computing, just persist)."} </LM_OUTPUT>

