<FEEDBACK>- Training stability and schedule
  - The covariance-decorrelation term is blowing up (Infinity). Compute it in float32 outside AMP, penalize only off-diagonal covariance, and ramp a smaller gamma. Add NaN/Inf checks per batch and skip/clip offending penalties.
  - Greatly extend training (epochs ~300) with early-stopping patience ~30 and a longer KL ramp (~20). Freeze W_prior longer during warmup (~20) before unfreezing.
  - Turn on batch-invariance: enable a nonzero MMD weight with a warmup ramp; compute kernels in fp32. Use a class-balanced batch sampler so each mini-batch contains multiple datasets; otherwise MMD is noisy or null.

- Decoder likelihood and initialization
  - Prefer NB with a log-link and explicit log-library-size offset (log mu = linear + log libsize) to avoid softmax-induced competition across genes; at minimum clamp mu/theta in fp32 to safe ranges and keep the NB loss out of autocast.
  - Normalize W_prior initialization by set size and equalize column norms so prior-aligned columns start on comparable scales to the free branch. Consider a learnable global temperature on decoder logits to prevent over-smooth softmax.

- Prior usage and bias control
  - Consume the curated, filtered membership and Laplacian artifacts produced in preprocessing (M_final.filtered.npz and L_model.filtered.npz) to guarantee exact gene×set order and set selection consistency, rather than recomputing alignment.
  - Regularize per-dataset gene biases (small L2) or recenter them each epoch to zero mean across datasets so they don’t absorb biological signal.

- Encoder conditioning and invariance
  - Reduce leakage of batch into z by moving FiLM conditioning to the decoder only, or detach gradient from the covariate modulation path in the encoder (use covariates as conditioning, not a learning signal for mu/logvar). Retain only log_library_size on the encoder if you need any covariate there.

- Loss design and weighting
  - Add free-bits (minimum KL per-dimension) to prevent posterior collapse and to keep both z_prior and z_free active.
  - Keep the L1 sparsity on z_prior per-sample then average over batch; drive its strength via the provided per-set weights with a single global scale. Monitor mean|z_prior| and ensure it’s not saturating to zero.

- Optimization details
  - Use LR warmup then cosine decay; set drop_last=True for more stable batch statistics in penalties. Create optimizer parameter groups to disable weight decay for biases and optionally for W_prior.

- Embedding/clustering selection (major impact on ARI)
  - Implement the planned kNN+Leiden grid with bootstrap stability and modularity under the 8–40 cluster constraint. Search across representations {z_concat, z_prior, z_free}, metrics {cosine/euclidean}, and k. Optionally reduce the concatenated latent with PCA (e.g., 50D) before kNN to denoise.
  - Learn or tune a scalar weighting between prior and free latents for clustering (rather than a fixed sqrt ratio), chosen by validation modularity/stability. Merge tiny clusters and perform majority-vote refinement on border cells.

- Numerics and logging
  - Keep NB NLL, MMD, and decor penalties in fp32 blocks; add guardrails that log and skip penalties when they produce NaN/Inf. Track and log z_prior sparsity, W_prior norms, and the (properly computed) Laplacian term each epoch.

- Artifacts
  - Persist posterior means (z_prior, z_free, z_concat) back into AnnData.obsm and save W_prior (masked), W_free, biases, theta, and full CONFIG for reproducibility and downstream summaries.</FEEDBACK>

