<LM_OUTPUT> {"role":"biology","feedback":"Clustering and selection\n- Remove or relax the small-cluster merge (min_cluster_size=30). Set to 10–15 or disable; otherwise rare PBMC types (e.g., DCs) get absorbed, hurting ARI and biology.\n- After refinement, recheck constraints (8–40 clusters) and recompute modularity/stability; reject solutions violating the range post-refinement.\n- Avoid hard pruning of graph edges (prune_threshold=0.05). Use 0.0–0.01 to prevent fragmentation that destabilizes Leiden.\n- Increase bootstrap robustness (n_boot=10) and report stability on the refined labels over the chosen graph.\n\nDEGs and biological coherence\n- Use one-sided marker detection: set rank_genes_groups(rankby_abs=False) and keep genes with logFC>0. Prefer positive markers for labels.\n- Relax filters to recover real immune markers: require pct_in≥0.2–0.25 and pct_out≤0.3–0.5; keep |log2FC|≥0.25. Maintain FDR<0.05.\n- Compute effect sizes on linear scale: for postfilters, use expm1(X) to recompute mean expressions and log2FC, ensuring consistency.\n- Increase marker list size per cluster (e.g., top 100–300 significant upregulated genes) and use that full list for enrichment; top-10 is underpowered and yields spurious sets (e.g., urogenital development in PBMCs).\n\nPathway/marker summaries\n- Prefer z_prior-based activities: ensure the AnnData used here has obsm['z_prior'] from the trained model (load the model’s output h5ad or add a separate z_prior.npy + metadata). If absent, write it during training and consume it here.\n- For enrichment fallback, keep background as used_in_model (already done), require overlap≥2 and q≤0.1 for reporting; optionally restrict sources to immune/hematopoietic collections for PBMCs.\n- Derive provisional labels from a curated PBMC marker dictionary (e.g., CD3D, MS4A1, LST1, S100A8/A9, NCAM1, KLRD1, CST3, FCGR3A, FCER1A) matched to DEGs, instead of the top enriched set name.\n\nMetrics\n- ARI computation is correct; also validate uniqueness of cell_id before merge and log n_test_used (already done). Add per-cluster test-set purity/homogeneity for diagnostics.\n\nImplementation notes\n- Ensure assignments and DEG computation use identical cell universes (no dropped cells due to outer concat); if concatenating preprocessed splits, verify shared var and fill-missing genes with zeros.\n- Log chosen k/resolution, pre/post-refinement cluster counts, and stability/modularity changes to aid debugging of ARI drops."} </LM_OUTPUT>

