Here is the feedback we got for generated code for downstream_analysis.py in the conversation:

<FEEDBACK>- Graph construction and similarity
  - Drop or greatly reduce prune_threshold (<=0.01) and avoid taking only the upper triangle; instead symmetrize weights as max(W, W.T) to retain connectivity and avoid fragmentation that hurts Leiden stability/ARI.
  - Add an SNN/Jaccard-weighted graph option (build kNN adjacency, weight edges by Jaccard of neighbor sets) and include it in the grid; SNN consistently improves discrete immune cell separation.
  - Do not per-dimension whiten the embedding by default; it can destroy calibrated variance from the VAE. If standardization is desired, compute statistics on the train split only, or test both “no-whiten + L2” vs “whiten + L2” as a grid choice.
  - Grid-search the neighbor metric (cosine vs euclidean) and expand k_grid adaptively (e.g., include round(sqrt(n)), round(0.5%–1% of n)) to better match dataset scale.

- Clustering selection and stability
  - Recompute stability on the refined labels over the final chosen graph and use this in scoring; current score ignores the effects of refinement.
  - Increase bootstrap replicates (e.g., n_boot=10) and run Leiden with multiple seeds per (k, res), aggregating stability across seeds.
  - Upweight test-set stability in the harmonic/geometric mean (e.g., 2:1) since ARI is evaluated on test; this remains unsupervised and directly targets the objective.
  - Enforce the cluster-count constraint strictly after refinement; reject candidates outside the 8–40 range instead of only downweighting them.
  - Add an unsupervised compactness criterion (e.g., silhouette in the latent space) as a tiebreaker with modularity to penalize overly diffuse clusters that depress ARI.

- Refinement policy
  - Lower or disable the small-cluster merge (min_cluster_size) and only merge if modularity increases; unconditional merges absorb rare immune populations (e.g., DCs) and reduce ARI.
  - For ambiguous-cell reassignment, vote over SNN core neighbors rather than kNN alone to avoid hubness-driven mislabels.

- DEG and biological signal (feeds back into labeling/enrichment coherence)
  - Use one-sided upregulated markers (rankby_abs=False) and relax thresholds (e.g., pct_in≥0.2–0.25, pct_out≤0.3–0.5, |log2FC|≥0.25) while keeping FDR<0.05 to recover canonical immune markers missed by strict filters.
  - Compute postfilter effect sizes on linear scale (expm1) before log2FC to avoid bias from log1p in low counts.
  - Increase marker list size used for enrichment (e.g., top 100–300 significant upregulated genes) to boost pathway/marker detection power and reduce spurious GO terms.

- Pathway/marker summaries
  - Prefer z_prior activities for top sets by ensuring obsm['z_prior'] is available to downstream (write from training and load here); fall back to enrichment only if absent.
  - In enrichment, require overlap≥2 and q≤0.1 for reporting to avoid biologically implausible labels that confuse interpretation and downstream decisions.

- ARI computation and robustness
  - Assert cell_id uniqueness in both metadata and INPUT_MOD1 before merging; detect and drop duplicates to prevent label mismatches diluting ARI.
  - Log and persist pre- vs post-refinement cluster counts, stability, and modularity, plus per-cluster test-set purity/homogeneity to diagnose ARI regressions.

- Efficiency/engineering
  - Cache neighbor indices per k (or use a single large k and derive subgraphs) to make the expanded grid feasible without runtime blowups, enabling broader search that can yield higher-ARI solutions.</FEEDBACK>

