[Notes]
[curated] Implements an end-to-end prior construction pipeline that harmonizes human gene symbols, computes batch-robust per-gene variance (library-size 1e4 normalize, log1p, median across adata.obs['dataset']), curates canonical MSigDB/GO/cell markers (human, evidence-filtered, immune/blood-biased) and NeST TF regulons, excludes MT-/RPS/RPL/unexpressed non-coding genes, overlap-controls via size/Jaccard with adaptive relaxation, scores sets by IC = mean variance × log10(size) to select 800–1500, builds an IDF-weighted L2-normalized gene×set CSR matrix and NeST-based undirected TF–target adjacency plus normalized Laplacian, computes source/size-scaled set weights, and writes standardized genes, symbol map, membership, set metadata (with normalized IC and column norms), regulatory matrices, weights, and a summary to /home/mcb/users/ekourb/singlecell_Agent/runsv2/results/intermediate_output/step_0/prior (metric 0.8226265030933464; gain: None).
[curated] We introduced a prior-aware, batch-invariant preprocessing pipeline that ingests RNA_count.h5ad with prior genes/gene-set/Laplacian (optional synonym map/weights), standardizes and synonym-collapses gene symbols, performs batch-wise QC and 1:1 prior alignment, preserves raw counts as layers["counts"] int32 CSR, normalizes to 1e4 and log1p, computes per-dataset HVGs, applies detection filtering (excluding MT/RPS/RPL), selects model genes as union(HVG, prior) capped at 7000 with ≥5 per set prioritized by nbatches/prior/mean, filters/realigns gene sets and prior matrices (M_final, L_model), builds covariates (one-hot domain/protocol/dataset + log_library_size) and deterministic stratified 80/10/10 splits, drops zero-train genes, validates artifacts and invariants (M: n_model_genes×n_kept_sets; L: n_model_genes×n_model_genes; n_model_genes ≤7000; set_min_size ≥5; n_sets_kept ≤1500; X float32; var.used_in_model; obsm["covariates"] float32; obs["split"]), and writes preprocess_all/train/val/test h5ad, M_final.filtered.npz, L_model.filtered.npz, prior_gene_sets_metadata.filtered.csv, and preprocess_metadata.json (coverage stats, indices, covariate schema, versions, checksum), yielding the listed files and Metric: 0.8226265030933464.
[step_0] Current Behavior
- End-to-end pipeline trains a prior-guided masked-decoder VAE on scRNA-seq with:
  - Encoder: MLP + FiLM by covariates; outputs mean/logvar for z = [z_prior, z_free].
  - Decoder: gene-set masked W_prior (initialized by membership × gene means), free component W_free, per-gene bias and per-dataset gene biases; NB likelihood with per-gene dispersion; library-size scaling via softmax.
  - Regularization: KL ramp, MMD(z_free | dataset) ramp for batch invariance, covariance decorrelation on z_concat, L1 group sparsity on mean|z_prior| with per-set weights, Laplacian smoothness on W_prior via prior graph.
  - Training: AdamW + cosine LR, AMP, grad clipping, warmup freeze on W_prior, early stopping on val ELBO.
- Data/prior handling:
  - Aligns genes to prior (standardized symbols), drops sets with <5 genes, subsets regulatory Laplacian, optional trim of sets to 800–1500 by size, maps per-set weights.
  - Uses normalized X for encoder inputs; raw counts + libsize for NB loss; covariates and dataset indices provided.
- Embedding/clustering:
  - Embeddings = concat[z_prior, z_free] means; z-score by train; balance prior/free energy.
  - Grid search over reps {z_concat, z_prior, z_free}, k-NN k∈{15,30,50,neighbors_k}, metric∈{cosine,euclidean}, Leiden/Louvain, resolutions.
  - Selects by stability (bootstrap ARI) + modularity under cluster-count constraints; fallback if none fit.
  - Evaluates ARI on test (labels for evaluation only), writes assignments and per-cluster summaries (DE genes; top gene sets from z_prior means; batch proportions).
- Notable caveats/bugs:
  - Laplacian penalty uses W_prior.detach().cpu().numpy(); no gradient flows to W_prior (penalty is constant wrt params).
  - Group sparsity scale likely double-applied: lambda_s defaults to group_l1_scale and is multiplied again by group_l1_scale in loss.
  - Memb mask converted to dense (toarray) for decoder buffers; may be memory-heavy for large G×S.
  - Val/test gene alignment assumes complete symbol overlap with train; KeyError risk if preprocessing diverges.

Step Change
- Introduces a biologically grounded, batch-aware VAE with pathway/marker masking, regulatory-graph prior, and batch-invariant free latents; implements full training, embedding, unsupervised clustering with stability search, and ARI evaluation; writes all artifacts and summaries with consistency checks.

Observed Outputs
- Files:
  - Best model: OUT_BEST_MODEL
  - Training logs/perf: OUT_TRAIN_LOGS, OUT_MODEL_PERF
  - Embedding + metadata: OUT_EMBEDDING (float32), OUT_EMBED_META (required cols validated)
  - Clusters: OUT_CLUSTER_ASSIGN (required cols validated), OUT_CLUSTER_METRICS (includes ari), OUT_CLUSTER_SUMMARY
  - Pipeline summary: OUT_PIPELINE_SUMMARY (cells, genes, n_sets, k_free, embedding_shape, best_epoch, best_val_elbo, ari_test, lib versions)
- Metrics/selection:
  - Best clustering chosen by stability + modularity with reported representation, k, metric, algorithm, resolution, stability, modularity.
  - Test ARI computed against cell_type on test split.
Metric: 0.8226265030933464, Gain: None
[step_0] Current Behavior
- Loads embedding.npy and embedding_metadata.csv; asserts shape/columns; uses metadata split for test-only ARI.
- Builds a cosine k-NN graph via Scanpy’s UMAP connectivities after per-dimension whitening and L2 row-normalization; prunes edges < 0.05; converts to weighted igraph.
- Grid-searches k ∈ {10,15,20,30,40,50} and Leiden resolution ∈ [0.1,1.2] step 0.1:
  - Runs Leiden (RBConfiguration) with weights.
  - Computes modularity and bootstrap stability (n_boot=5, sample_frac=0.8) globally and within test indices (if ≥10 cells).
  - Scores by harmonic mean of global/test stability; deprioritizes solutions with clusters outside [8,40] (×0.5); tiebreak by modularity.
- Refines best membership:
  - Merges clusters < 30 cells into nearest centroid.
  - kNN (k=k_best) core detection (core_threshold=0.6) and majority-vote reassignment for non-core cells; relabels to contiguous IDs.
- Writes cluster_assignments.csv with cell_id, predicted_cluster, split.
- Computes ARI on test using cell_type from INPUT_MOD1; writes cluster_metrics.json with ARI, n_test_used, and chosen k/res/stability/modularity.
- Loads preprocessed train/val/test AnnData, concatenates; computes DEGs per predicted_cluster:
  - Filters genes by used_in_model and protein_coding (if present); Wilcoxon with BH correction, requires p_adj<0.05, pct_in≥0.1, pct_out≤0.1, |LFC|≥0.5; fallback to simple mean LFC if Scanpy fails.
- Pathway/marker summarization:
  - Loads prior genes, sets, and membership; maps gene symbols via standardized symbols and optional alias map; background restricted to modeling genes present; hypergeometric enrichment with BH FDR; set size 10–500; top 10 per cluster.
  - If adata.obsm["z_prior"] exists, uses per-cluster mean activity to rank top 10 sets instead.
- Computes per-cluster batch proportions over available fields (domain/protocol/dataset).
- Writes cluster_summary.json with size, top_markers, top_gene_sets (qval/overlap or z_prior score), batch_proportions, and provisional_label (top set name).

Step Change
- Introduces a complete downstream pipeline for clustering an external latent embedding, stability-driven parameter selection, refinement, ARI evaluation, DEG computation, prior-based enrichment (or z_prior summarization), batch composition, and standardized JSON/CSV outputs.

