<FEEDBACK>{"role":"data_science","feedback":"Actionable changes to boost ARI via preprocessing correctness, prior alignment, and artifact schema compliance:\n- Fix HVG timing and scope: compute HVGs before prior alignment on the full standardized/collapsed gene space and with layer='counts' (seurat_v3 expects raw counts). Then align to the prior and keep HVGs even if not in any prior set by padding M (zero rows) and L (zero rows/cols) for those genes. This recovers informative non-prior HVGs and avoids prior-induced bias in HVGs.\n- Eliminate leakage: perform the stratified split first; fit all train-dependent transforms only on train (detection thresholds, HVGs, residualization coefficients, gene z-scoring, PCA loadings) and apply to val/test by index mapping. Persist the train-fitted parameters in metadata.\n- Enforce spec MT filter: use a hard percent.mt > 20% cutoff (not group-adaptive) while keeping the robust within-group 1%/99% count trimming and 200/7000 feature bounds.\n- Tighten detection policy for prior genes: require detected > 0 for all genes (including prior-covered) to survive filtering; keep the relaxed fraction threshold for prior genes if desired, but don’t pass completely unobserved genes through (they later become zero-train anyway).\n- Use prior’s weighting for gene-set activity: don’t re-scale columns by 1/size. Multiply X by the provided membership matrix as-is (IDF-weighted), then L2-normalize gene-set columns or z-score GS features on the train split before PCA. This better reflects prior construction and stabilizes PCA.\n- Residualization robustness: fit the covariate regression (intercept + one-hot domain/protocol/dataset + log_library_size) on train only, using ridge (CV’d alpha) instead of OLS to avoid overfitting/collinearity. Persist coefficients and apply to val/test.\n- PCA dimensionality: hard-cap n_components (e.g., 50) and assert saved embedding has that dimension. The current summary shows 955 dims, implying PCA didn’t reduce; enforce/validate reduction to avoid noisy k-means inputs.\n- Clustering outputs contract: write cluster_assignments.csv with column name predicted_cluster (not cluster), and write cluster_metrics.json with the exact key \"ari\" holding ARI on the test split only. This aligns with the evaluator and prevents metric drop from key/name mismatches.\n- Gene-cap fairness: when enforcing MIN_PER_SET_COVERAGE under the MODEL_GENE_CAP, iterate sets in a round-robin or priority queue so early sets don’t monopolize the budget. Then fill remaining slots by a global rank (prior_set_counts, HVG batch robustness, mean expression).\n- HVG per-batch union: ensure per-dataset HVG union is actually realized (batch_key restricted to observed train batches) and gracefully handle single-batch cases.\n- Persist transforms and splits explicitly: add a data_splits.json containing split indices and the final model gene indices; persist train-fitted scalers (gene-level mean/var), ridge coefficients, PCA components, and prior gene/set index maps.\n- Store raw for DE: set ad_all.raw = log1p CPM X to support DE downstream while keeping layers['counts'] as integer CSR.\n- Minor correctness: fix in-set indexing when building the MIN_PER_SET_COVERAGE pool using M_matched[cand, s].A.ravel() > 0 to avoid shape mismatches; keep all dtype checks and invariants in place."}</FEEDBACK>


