<LM_OUTPUT> {"role":"model","feedback":"Key fixes to hit the intended prior-guided, batch-invariant VAE and stabilize training:\n- Stabilize decorrelation penalty (source of Infinity):\n  - Compute covariance penalty in float32 outside AMP: with torch.cuda.amp.autocast(False): z32 = z.float(); use z32 for cov; return penalty in float32.\n  - Penalize only off-diagonals: cov = (z32 - z32.mean(0)).T @ (z32 - z32.mean(0)) / max(1, B-1); off = cov - torch.diag(torch.diag(cov)); decor = (off**2).mean().\n  - Lower gamma to 1e-3 and optionally ramp 0→1e-3 over 20 epochs.\n- Match training schedule to plan (underfitting now): set CONFIG epochs=300, early_stopping_patience=30, beta_kl_final=0.5 with beta_ramp_epochs=20, warmup_freeze_prior_epochs=20.\n- Turn on batch-invariance: set mmd_weight=1e-2 and mmd_ramp_epochs=20; compute MMD in float32 (disable autocast around kernel) to avoid fp16 underflow.\n- Architecture per spec: hidden_dims=[1024,512,256] with GELU+LayerNorm+Dropout(0.1); keep FiLM modulation.\n- Decoder init and scaling:\n  - Normalize W_prior init by set size to avoid scale bias: init_w = memb.multiply(init_gene_means[:,None] / np.maximum(1, memb.getnnz(1))[:,None]).\n  - Keep softmax+libsize NB path in float32 (disable autocast for nb_nll) and clamp mu,theta to [1e-6, 1e6] before logs.\n- Losses per plan:\n  - Enable Laplacian smoothness with laplacian_alpha=1e-3; compute on-device using torch.sparse.mm for stability/perf.\n  - Group sparsity: apply L1 on z_prior per-sample then mean over batch; use the provided per-set weights λ_s directly; remove any extra global scaling in the loss term except λ0.\n  - Optional: split KL weights for prior/free (beta_prior=beta_free=beta by default) to tune balance if prior dims >> free dims.\n- Optimization:\n  - Add LR warmup (e.g., 10 epochs linear to 1e-3) then cosine decay; keep AdamW(betas=(0.9,0.999), wd=1e-4), grad_clip=1.0, AMP on main forward but off for numerically sensitive losses (NB, MMD, decor).\n  - Shuffle with drop_last=True for more stable batch stats in penalties.\n- Monitoring/guardrails:\n  - After each step, check for isnan/isinf in losses; if triggered, skip penalty terms for that batch and log counts. Log mean|z_prior| and W_prior norms each epoch.\n- ZINB option: add a per-gene dropout gate pi_g via logit parameter and train NB vs ZINB by monitoring val NLL; enable ZINB only if it reduces val recon by a threshold.\n- Inference/artifacts:\n  - Save posterior means z_prior, z_free, z_concat to obsm; persist W_prior (masked), W_free, b_g, θ_g, and full CONFIG.\nThese changes address the numeric instability, enforce batch invariance, align capacity and schedule with the plan, and should lift ARI beyond the current underfit regime."} </LM_OUTPUT>

