|NOTES|: [Recent Steps]
step=0 action=exploit success=True ari=0.8226265030933464 gain=None stagnation=0 targets=data_preprocess.py,prior_construction.py,model_training.py,downstream_analysis.py
step=1 action=exploit success=True ari=0.4331931714142928 gain=-0.3894333316790536 stagnation=1 targets=model_training.py,downstream_analysis.py,data_preprocess.py

[Notes]
[curated] Introduces a full pipeline that loads embedding.npy/metadata, builds a cosine k-NN graph via Scanpy UMAP connectivities after per-dimension whitening and L2 normalization (pruning edges <0.05; converted to weighted igraph), grid-searches k={10,15,20,30,40,50} and Leiden resolution 0.1–1.2 with weights optimizing harmonic-mean bootstrap stability (deprioritizing cluster counts outside 8–40; tiebreak by modularity), refines clusters (merge <30 cells; k_best core=0.6 majority-vote), writes cluster_assignments.csv (cell_id, predicted_cluster, split), computes test ARI from INPUT_MOD1 and writes cluster_metrics.json (ari, n_test_used, k, resolution, modularity, stability_global/test), computes DEGs per cluster (Wilcoxon BH with filters; fallback LFC), summarizes markers/pathways by prior gene-set enrichment with BH FDR (size 10–500; or z_prior), reports batch proportions, and writes cluster_summary.json using PREPROCESS_* and PRIOR_OUTPUT_DIR artifacts, achieving metric 0.8226265030933464.
[curated] Pipeline still builds priors (from fixed paths with hard Cell_marker_Human.xlsx parsing), constructs standardized genes, filters/deduplicates and IC-scores 800–1500 sets, outputs float32 CSR membership (n_genes×n_sets, L2-normalized columns) plus regulatory adjacency/Laplacian (n_genes×n_genes, float32), and writes/asserts artifacts with summary, but now supports env-overridable input_mod1/prior_output_dir (case-insensitive), optional mirroring via prior_output_dir_mirror or auto /step_0/→/step_1/, robust marker Excel load with skip+log on failure, hardened Laplacian numerics and CSV check, expanded summary to list adj/laplacian, and mirroring of all artifacts; outputs/invariants under PRIOR_OUTPUT_DIR remain the same (mirror duplicates if enabled), unreadable/missing markers no longer fail (n_sets_selected may drop but stays adaptive), numerical outputs otherwise unchanged; Metric 0.4331931714142928, Gain -0.3894333316790536.
[curated] The pipeline now standardizes symbols; performs QC and batch-aware cell filtering stratified by domain||protocol||dataset with a strict 20% MT cutoff; moves the stratified split before HVG and computes HVGs on train-only raw counts (allowing non-prior HVGs); normalizes to 10k CPM + log1p while preserving int32 CSR counts; selects model genes as (HVG ∪ prior) ∩ detected ∩ non-technical with expanded technical flags and train-only detection, capped via metadata-informed global ranking and round-robin across top-priority sets; adds one-hot covariates (domain, protocol, dataset, donor, sample, chemistry, kit, lane) excluding log_library_size; computes per-gene train-only mean/std with an X_zscore layer; reindexes/pads prior matrices to model genes; and writes split h5ad plus aligned prior artifacts and JSON metadata mirrored to step_1, yielding metric 0.4331931714142928 (gain −0.3894333316790536).
[step_1] Current Behavior
- Loads preprocessed splits and filtered prior artifacts (membership M, Laplacian L, gene set metadata) from PREPROCESS_METADATA to ensure exact gene ordering across train/val/test.
- VAE with FiLM-conditioned encoder (covariates detached to reduce leakage) and masked decoder:
  - Decoder enforces pathway/marker mask on W_prior, adds free factors W_free, per-gene bias, per-dataset gene bias, global logit scale.
  - Negative binomial likelihood with log-link and explicit log-library-size offset; dispersion via softplus.
- Regularization:
  - Group L1 on z_prior with optional per-set weights.
  - Laplacian smoothness on masked W_prior via torch.sparse mm on GPU.
  - Off-diagonal covariance penalty on [z_prior, z_free].
  - Batch-invariance via MMD on z_free across dataset indices.
  - Small L2 on dataset bias to prevent absorbing biology.
- Training:
  - BalancedBatchSampler to balance datasets within each batch.
  - Warmup: freeze W_prior for 20 epochs, ramp beta KL and MMD weight.
  - AdamW with no weight decay on biases and W_prior; LR warmup then cosine via LambdaLR; AMP + grad clipping; early stopping.
