- Add doublet detection and filter/tag before splitting. Since doublets degrade clustering quality, run Scrublet (per dataset||protocol group to account for library-size/batch effects), add obs['doublet_score'] and obs['is_doublet'], and either remove high-confidence doublets (e.g., adaptive p-value threshold per group) or at least exclude them from train/val/test splits. Log counts in the QC report.

- Provide zero-inflation diagnostics for likelihood selection. Compute and persist per-gene var['zero_fraction_train'] from train counts and a global mean in uns; this enables a principled NB vs ZINB switch downstream and stabilizes reconstruction, which improves latent structure and ARI.

- Make HVG selection more batch-robust. Compute highly variable genes with batch_key set to the combined dataset||protocol (not dataset alone), and take the union across those batches. Persist var['highly_variable_nbatches'] as you do, but ensure it reflects the combined key; this reduces protocol-specific noise in the HVG pool.

- Strengthen prior coverage during gene capping. When enforcing MODEL_GENE_CAP, prioritize genes by (a) HVG flag, (b) prior degree, (c) train mean expression, but guarantee a minimum per-set coverage using the already filtered set list (post intersection) rather than all sets. Also bias the round-robin order by per-set “activity” proxies (e.g., mean expression of set members in train) to keep informative sets represented.

- Persist filtered set weights aligned to kept sets. Derive per-set weights scaled by 1/sqrt(set_size_after_intersection) (and optionally information-content from prior metadata), save them alongside M_final/L_model (e.g., artifacts['set_weights_filtered_json']), and record the kept set IDs. This allows training to apply calibrated group sparsity on z_prior, improving pathway alignment and downstream ARI.

- Tighten technical and ambient contamination handling. 
  - Tag immunoglobulin constant/variable genes (IGHG*, IGKC, IGLC*, IGHV/IGKV/IGLV) as technical-like and exclude them from modeling but keep for QC summaries.
  - Add an ambient RNA proxy (e.g., fraction of counts in top N ambient genes per dataset/protocol) to obs, and optionally filter extreme ambient-contaminated cells; log in QC.

- Add RBC-heavy cell filtering. In addition to excluding hemoglobin genes from modeling, compute per-cell hemoglobin fraction and remove cells above a high threshold (e.g., >5–10% HBB/HBA fraction) as likely erythrocyte contamination; record removals in the QC report.

- Stabilize splits and categories across runs. Persist obs['batch_index_dataset'] (int-coded dataset), obs['batch_index_group'] (int-coded domain||protocol||dataset) and the categorical orderings used to build all covariate one-hots in preprocess_metadata. This eliminates accidental category reordering and supports deterministic balanced batching/MMD across the combined batch key.

- Expose library size as an optional numeric covariate. You already compute obs['log_library_size']; store it in obsm (e.g., obsm['covariates_numeric'] with standardized values using train stats) so training can append it to the encoder covariates if configured, while keeping it out of the main categorical covariates to avoid leakage by default.

- Save per-gene/train detection and dispersion proxies. Persist var-level train-only mean, variance, and CV (you already save mean/std for X_zscore); include var['detected_train'] counts. These stabilize initialization/ranking and allow downstream to de-prioritize noisy genes within the cap in a reproducible way.

- Guard against memory blowups during dense conversions. Where you currently call toarray() for train subsets (e.g., HVG fallback, X_zscore computation), gate by size and use chunked operations/sparse-safe statistics to prevent excessive densification on large datasets; unstable numerics or OOM during preprocessing can silently alter the gene set, hurting ARI reproducibility.

- Record and enforce prior set count bounds. If the intersection yields <800 or >1500 sets, rank by information content/coverage and trim/pad (as per PLAN) to the 800–1500 window; persist both the decision and ranking criteria. Keeping set dimensionality in a sweet spot stabilizes z_prior and subsequent clustering.</FEEDBACK>


