- Fix encoder inputs and covariates to reduce leakage and stabilize learning:
  - Feed the z-scored log1p CPM layer you saved during preprocessing (layers["X_zscore"]) to the encoder instead of raw X; keep raw integer counts only as the NB target and libsize offset.
  - Restrict FiLM covariates to high-level batch fields (domain, protocol, dataset); drop donor/sample/kit/lane to avoid encoding nuisance IDs that hurt invariance. Keep log-library-size only as a decoder offset, not as an encoder covariate.

- Capacity and schedules aligned to the task:
  - Increase encoder width/depth to match the specified design (e.g., [1024,512,256]) and expand k_free to ~32 so z_free can absorb residuals without swamping z_prior.
  - Warm up longer with W_prior frozen (~20 epochs), ramp β to 0.5 over the same window, and ramp group sparsity from 0→λ0 after unfreezing, rather than applying L1 on z_prior from step 1.

- Make the prior branch identifiable and competitive with the free branch:
  - Constrain W_prior to be nonnegative (e.g., softplus parameterization or ReLU + mask) to respect membership semantics; if you keep it unconstrained, at least add a penalty for negative masked entries.
