  - Scale group L1 weights by 1/sqrt(set_size) to avoid over-penalizing large pathways; keep a global λ0 (e.g., 1e-3) and ramp it.

- Likelihood health and dataset biases:
  - Add an automatic ZINB switch: if the train zero fraction is high (>~0.6), learn a per-gene dropout head π_g; otherwise use NB. This prevents mis-specified likelihoods on sparse protocols.
  - Increase dataset_bias_l2 by an order of magnitude (e.g., ~1e-4) so per-dataset gene biases don’t absorb biological variability.

- Batch construction that actually balances confounders:
  - Balance minibatches by the combined dataset×protocol×domain key and oversample minority groups within an epoch to equalize contributions; current sampler can under-cover long tails.
  - Ensure each epoch draws ~ceil(n_samples/batch_size) batches with replacement to avoid systematic dropout of samples when groups are many.

- Regularization targeting disentanglement instead of suppression:
  - Apply the covariance penalty only to z_free (off-diagonals), not to [z_prior|z_free]; optionally add a cross-cov penalty between z_prior and z_free to encourage separation without dampening z_prior signal.

- Early stopping on the true objective:
