[Notes]
[curated] The pipeline loads an embedding; builds symmetric max(W,W.T) cell graphs via UMAP connectivities or SNN (Jaccard over kNN) with cosine/euclidean metrics and optional train-split whitening/pruning; runs a multi-seed grid over {k, resolution, graph method, neighbor metric, whitening, prune} using Leiden with modularity-improving small-cluster merges and SNN-weighted reassignment; selects by a 2:1 test-weighted harmonic mean of bootstrap stabilities (n_boot=10) plus across-seed ARI and silhouette while enforcing 8–40 clusters; computes test ARI and per-cluster purity; outputs deduplicated cluster_assignments.csv, cluster_metrics.json (ari, stability_global/test, silhouette, k, resolution, graph/method details, test_cluster_purity, etc.), and cluster_summary.json (sizes, upregulated-only DEGs with FDR<0.05, pct_in≥0.2, pct_out≤0.5, |LFC|≥0.25, top 200; top gene sets from z_prior or BH q≤0.1 overlap≥2 top 10; batch proportions; provisional labels), mirrors to step_1, returns a normalized embedding and uses local graph rebuilds in bootstraps, with increased runtime, yielding Metric 0.4331931714142928 and Gain -0.3894333316790536.
[curated] Pipeline builds standardized gene list/alias map (excluding MT/RPS/RPL and unexpressed non-coding), loads and size-filters MSigDB/GO/markers/NeST to 800–1500 de-duplicated IC-ranked sets, constructs IDF-like weighted, column L2-normalized membership matrix and NeST-derived TF-target undirected adjacency plus normalized Laplacian (all float32 CSR), computes per-set weights and writes metadata/summary with checks; step change only generalizes artifact mirroring to multiple destinations (env prior_output_dir_mirror and auto step_{k+1}/prior and step_{k+2}/prior or step_1/step_2) with best-effort copy, .npz reload/resave fallback, dir creation, and per-mirror error skipping, leaving primary artifacts unchanged and adding mirrored copies; Metric: 0.4204504375636808, Gain: -0.4021760655296656.
[curated] This update introduces RBC/doublet (Scrublet per dataset||protocol) and ambient filtering; unifies train-only detection to 0.005 before HVG (now on detection-filtered genes with batch_key=dataset||protocol, sparse-safe); changes technical exclusions to MT/RIBO/IG (hemoglobin allowed); revises gene/set selection to prioritize weighted prior coverage with activity- and coverage-balanced prior set retention (800–1500) and persists size-normalized set weights (mirrored to step_1/step_2); restricts covariates to non-leaky (domain/protocol/dataset) while adding covariates_full/batch3, numeric standardized log_library_size, and stable batch indices; stores train-only encoder input stats (removes X_zscore), expands diagnostics/metadata, and mirrors artifacts to step_1/step_2—however it contains a critical regression (collapse_duplicate_symbols undefined) and may reduce cells and alter the gene set, with metric 0.4204504375636808 (gain −0.4021760655296656).
[step_2] Current Behavior
- Prior-guided masked-decoder VAE with FiLM covariates built from one-hot domain/protocol/dataset; z = [z_prior (pathway/marker), z_free].
- Decoder supports NB or auto-switched ZINB (train zero fraction > 0.6), dataset-specific bias, global logit temperature; W_prior masked by gene-set membership.
- Training: warmup freeze of W_prior, then unfreeze; losses = NB/ZINB NLL + β KL (free-bits) + group L1 on z_prior (size-normalized λ_s, ramped post-unfreeze) + Laplacian on W_prior + decorrelation on z_free (+ optional cross-cov) + MMD on z_free across combined batch groups (dataset|protocol|domain) + L2 on dataset biases + prior identifiability (nonnegativity on W_prior, column-norm ~1, orthogonality W_free⊥W_prior). End-epoch column renorm of W_prior.
- Optimizer: AdamW with param groups (W_free higher WD, W_prior/bias no WD) and LR warmup→cosine; grad clip + AMP. BalancedBatchSampler samples per combined group with replacement.
- Embedding: concatenate mean [z_prior, z_free]; clustering via scanpy neighbors + Leiden on a small grid (k=neighbors_k, cosine; res ∈ {0.4,0.8,1.2}; α reweight for z_prior when concatenated). Selection by silhouette (subsample if large), tie-break by connectivity density; tiny clusters merged to nearest large.
- Artifacts mirrored automatically from step_0 to step_1 and step_2.

Step Change
- Data prep: replaced precomputed obsm covariates with consistent cross-split one-hot domain/protocol/dataset; added combined group_idx for sampler/MMD; prefer X_zscore if present.
- Model/decoder: added ZINB branch (gene-level π), larger numerical clamps, explicit logit_scale.
- Objectives: added/changed
  - Group L1 ramp (post-unfreeze) with size-normalized λ_s.
  - MMD now over combined group_idx (was dataset).
  - Decorrelation only on z_free; optional cross-cov z_prior↔z_free (default off).
  - Prior identifiability: nonnegativity, column-norm, W_free–W_prior orthogonality.
  - Laplacian kept on masked W_prior; end-epoch unit-norm projection.
- Sampler: new BalancedBatchSampler balancing combined group with replacement; exact ceil(N/batch) batches; train loader no drop_last.
- Optimizer: separate WD for W_free (higher), zero WD for W_prior/bias.
- Schedules/hparams: epochs 300→200; LR warmup 10→20; free-bits 0.02→0.05; dataset_bias_l2 1e-5→1e-4; added ramps (mmd_ramp_epochs, group_l1_ramp_epochs) and penalties (prior_nonneg, prior_colnorm, orthogonality); cross_decor param added (default 0).
- Validation/early stop: now selects by full regularized val objective; logs keep key name best_val_elbo for compatibility.
- Clustering: grid reduced (k fixed, cosine only); selection metric switched from bootstrap stability to silhouette; metrics JSON now reports silhouette (not stability).
- I/O: unified mirror_to_steps() copies all artifacts to step_1 and step_2; checkpoint includes use_zinb flag.

Observed Outputs
- best_model.pt saved with decoder_artifacts including use_zinb and projected W_prior; W_prior columns near unit norm; monitors in logs: mean_abs_zprior, wprior_colnorm_mean≈1, logits_free_frac.
- training_logs.json history now includes train/val regularizer terms and val_total; model_performance.json retains best_val_elbo key (now full-objective).
- embedding.npy unchanged format; embedding_metadata.csv unchanged required columns.
- cluster_assignments.csv unchanged schema; cluster_metrics.json now contains ari plus silhouette, chosen_representation, k, metric, resolution, alpha_prior_weight, n_clusters.
- All artifacts mirrored to step_1 and step_2 directories.
Metric: 0.4204504375636808, Gain: -0.4021760655296656
[step_2] Current Behavior
- Step 1 selected clustering by weighted-harmonic mean of bootstrap stability (test:global = 2:1), with across-seed ARI and silhouette as minor add-ons. It searched over {method ∈ [umap,snn], metric ∈ [cosine,euclidean], k grid, whitening, prune}, enforced 8–40 clusters, refined via SNN voting, and wrote ARI/diagnostics. Pathway enrichment used DEGs or z_prior if present.
- Bootstrap used n_boot=10, sample_frac=0.8. No explicit batch-alignment control, no train-anchored graph, no post-hoc split. No prior/free scaling. DEGs used fixed pct_in/pct_out columns. z_prior set names came only from sets_meta.

Step Change
- Scoring and selection:
  - Now optimizes 0.5*(0.6*sil_test + 0.4*sil_global) + 0.5*stability, minus 0.1*batch-alignment penalty (AMI with dataset/protocol on test), promoting batch-invariance.
  - Light bootstrap (n_boot=3, sample_frac=0.7) for speed; seeds reduced to 2; metric fixed to cosine.
  - Best seed chosen by combined silhouette (0.6 test, 0.4 global). Tight cluster-count gate remains (8–40).
- Graph/normalization:
  - Optional whitening fit on train only; pruning supports numeric or “p10” percentile; graph caching across grid.
  - Train-anchored variant (edges must touch train) evaluated and adopted if it improves score.
- Embedding prior/free balance:
  - Optional alpha scaling for z_prior dims (first n_sets) if embedding metadata provides n_sets and k_free; alpha grid = [0.5,1.0,2.0] when applicable.
- Refinement and robustness:
  - refine_assignments adds centroid fallback when SNN votes are ambiguous; merges tiny clusters only if modularity increases.
  - Optional single-pass large-cluster split (KMeans=2) applied only if both modularity and test-silhouette improve.
- Metrics and diagnostics:
  - Final test-only stability computed on the selected solution; metrics JSON includes warning_low_stability if stability_test<0.5.
  - ARI evaluation adds test coverage check.
  - DEG ranking more robust to column naming; adds mean_in_cpm and flexible pct column detection.
  - z_prior set naming can use persisted z_prior column map if available.

Observed Outputs
- cluster_metrics.json now includes:
  - resolution, k, modularity, stability_global, stability_test, silhouette, graph_method, neighbor_metric=“cosine”, whiten, prune_threshold, alpha_prior_scale, anchored_train_graph, n_clusters, warning_low_stability, test_cluster_purity.
- cluster_assignments may reflect:
  - Improved batch mixing (due to AMI penalty and anchoring).
  - Occasional additional subclusters from the optional split, still within 8–40.
- cluster_summary.json:
  - Top sets may come from z_prior with explicit column-to-set mapping when available; DEG-based enrichment remains with BH-FDR and corrected background.
- Runtime likely reduced (lighter bootstrap, graph caching), with added robustness to batch effects and ambiguous assignments.
