- Do not exclude immunoglobulin genes from modeling:
  - Excluding IG genes (IGHV/IGHG/IGKC/IGLC/IGKV/IGLV) removes key B-cell markers and can collapse separability of lymphoid subsets, hurting ARI. Keep the exclusion limited to MT and ribosomal (RPS/RPL/MRPS/MRPL) per spec; retain IG for modeling but continue to tag them for QC.

- Finalize all QC-based cell removals before splitting:
  - Move doublet and ambient filtering to precede the train/val/test stratified split so each split preserves per-batch representation after removals. This avoids depleted groups in val/test and improves cluster comparability and ARI on the test split.

- Make low-detection filtering less train-myopic to avoid dropping test-informative genes:
  - Compute the 0.5% detection filter over all cells (or use a union criterion: keep a gene if it meets the threshold in train OR, more leniently, in any dataset/protocol group). Keep HVG selection train-only to prevent leakage. This preserves rare/test-skewed markers and improves downstream clustering resolution.

- Align per-set weights with what training actually consumes:
