<LM_OUTPUT> {"role":"model","feedback":"Issues and targeted fixes to align training with the design and improve prior use/batch invariance:\n\n- Z-score encoder inputs by train-only stats (missing):\n  - In prepare_data(), read preprocess_metadata[\"encoder_preferences\"][\"input_stats\"] (mean_key, std_key), fetch train means/stds from ad_train.var, and apply to all splits: X = (X - mean) / std. Or create ad.layers['X_zscore'] at load time and keep using it. Remove the current fallback to raw X.\n\n- Use filtered set weights (avoid double size-normalization):\n  - Load md[\"artifacts\"][\"set_weights_filtered_json\"] if present and map by set_id in sets_meta_df to build lambda_s. Do not divide again by sqrt(set_size). Keep a single size-normalization (already applied in the filtered weights).\n\n- Make MMD effective (currently ~0 due to 1-sample groups):\n  - Compute MMD over dataset_idx (db) instead of the fine-grained group_idx (gb): replace mmd_between_groups(z_free, gb) with mmd_between_groups(z_free, db) in both train/val.\n  - Ensure ≥2 samples per dataset in each batch: in BalancedBatchSampler, build groups by dataset_idx for sampling (keep group_idx only for balancing order if needed) and set per_group = max(2, ceil(batch_size / n_datasets)).\n\n- Prevent free branch from dominating (logits_free_frac ~0.99):\n  - Add W_free column norm control analogous to W_prior: after each epoch, L2-normalize W_free columns; and add a small column-norm penalty like prior_colnorm_penalty to W_free.\n  - Reduce k_free from 32 to 16 (CONFIG[\"latent_free_dims\"]=16) or add L2 penalty on z_free magnitude (e.g., + 1e-4 * mean(z_free^2)).\n  - Lower group_l1_scale to 3e-4 and ramp over more epochs (e.g., group_l1_ramp_epochs=30) to avoid over-suppressing z_prior early, or freeze W_free for the first 20–30 epochs (set requires_grad=False then unfreeze) so the model must first use the prior branch.\n  - Optionally split KL by branch: apply a 1.5–2.0× multiplier to KL on z_free relative to z_prior.\n\n- Feed numeric covariates to the encoder FiLM (missing):\n  - Concatenate standardized log_library_size (from preprocess obsm['covariates_numeric'] or recomputed) to the one-hot domain/protocol/dataset when building Covtr/Covha/Covte so cov_dim includes this numeric effect.\n\n- Minor stability/consistency:\n  - When loading set weights, prefer id-based mapping and fall back to positional only if no set_id exists; log the effective lambda_s mean.\n  - Keep Laplacian on masked W_prior, but increase laplacian_alpha slightly (e.g., 3e-3) if prior columns remain noisy after the above changes.\n\nImplement the above and re-run; monitor: (1) logits_free_frac target ~0.6–0.8, (2) mean_abs_zprior not collapsing, (3) nonzero train/val MMD, and (4) ARI on test."} </LM_OUTPUT>

