[step_2] Current Behavior
- Step 1 selected clustering by weighted-harmonic mean of bootstrap stability (test:global = 2:1), with across-seed ARI and silhouette as minor add-ons. It searched over {method ∈ [umap,snn], metric ∈ [cosine,euclidean], k grid, whitening, prune}, enforced 8–40 clusters, refined via SNN voting, and wrote ARI/diagnostics. Pathway enrichment used DEGs or z_prior if present.
- Bootstrap used n_boot=10, sample_frac=0.8. No explicit batch-alignment control, no train-anchored graph, no post-hoc split. No prior/free scaling. DEGs used fixed pct_in/pct_out columns. z_prior set names came only from sets_meta.

Step Change
- Scoring and selection:
  - Now optimizes 0.5*(0.6*sil_test + 0.4*sil_global) + 0.5*stability, minus 0.1*batch-alignment penalty (AMI with dataset/protocol on test), promoting batch-invariance.
  - Light bootstrap (n_boot=3, sample_frac=0.7) for speed; seeds reduced to 2; metric fixed to cosine.
  - Best seed chosen by combined silhouette (0.6 test, 0.4 global). Tight cluster-count gate remains (8–40).
- Graph/normalization:
  - Optional whitening fit on train only; pruning supports numeric or “p10” percentile; graph caching across grid.
  - Train-anchored variant (edges must touch train) evaluated and adopted if it improves score.
- Embedding prior/free balance:
  - Optional alpha scaling for z_prior dims (first n_sets) if embedding metadata provides n_sets and k_free; alpha grid = [0.5,1.0,2.0] when applicable.
- Refinement and robustness:
  - refine_assignments adds centroid fallback when SNN votes are ambiguous; merges tiny clusters only if modularity increases.
  - Optional single-pass large-cluster split (KMeans=2) applied only if both modularity and test-silhouette improve.
- Metrics and diagnostics:
  - Final test-only stability computed on the selected solution; metrics JSON includes warning_low_stability if stability_test<0.5.
  - ARI evaluation adds test coverage check.
  - DEG ranking more robust to column naming; adds mean_in_cpm and flexible pct column detection.
  - z_prior set naming can use persisted z_prior column map if available.

Observed Outputs
- cluster_metrics.json now includes:
