<LM_OUTPUT> {"role": "biology", "feedback": "Clustering and selection: (1) In choose_best_params, add an explicit batch-balance term based on per-cluster entropy of dataset/protocol (size-weighted mean entropy) and penalize low entropy instead of AMI; this is more stable across unbalanced splits and avoids degenerate penalties when a batch is constant. (2) In refine_assignments, use a size-adaptive minimum cluster size: min_cluster_size = max(15, int(0.005 * n_cells)) to prevent tiny, low-quality clusters on larger datasets. (3) After selecting the final solution, run a targeted within-cluster re-cluster for clusters showing heterogeneous immune states by markers (e.g., DC clusters mixing pDC/ASDC): rebuild a kNN using only lineage/marker genes for that lineage and apply a single Leiden pass; accept the split only if test-silhouette improves. Diagnostics/metrics: (4) In write_cluster_metrics, omit warning_low_stability when stability is not computed (fields set to 0.0 now always trigger a spurious warning); if a quick diagnostic is desired, compute test-only stability with n_boot=3 and record it. (5) Log additional test diagnostics without affecting selection: normalized mutual information (NMI) and mean per-cluster batch entropy. DEG quality and biological coherence: (6) Make DE testing batch-aware by computing per-dataset (and/or per-protocol) Wilcoxon tests and combining p-values across batches (e.g., Fisher’s method) before applying current effect-size and pct filters; fall back to single-cell DE only when a cluster lacks ≥2 batch replicates. (7) Keep your effect-size screen but also require auROC ≥ 0.6 per gene (scanpy provides scores) to improve marker robustness; retain the existing CPM floor. (8) For clusters with atypical top markers for their provisional label (e.g., naive CD8 T with SFRP5/NRCAM), flag them and re-evaluate resolution locally (or merge with the nearest immunologically coherent neighbor) if their within-cluster marker concordance is low (e.g., median pairwise Jaccard of top-50 markers < 0.2). Pathway/marker summaries: (9) When z_prior is available, rank sets by signed mean activity (not absolute) and record direction; cap marker-derived sets to at most half of the top-10 and fill the remainder with non-marker (GO/Reactome/MSigDB) pathways to reduce circularity. (10) De-duplicate reported top sets by removing those with Jaccard overlap > 0.8 to a higher-ranked set. (11) Require concordance between z_prior top sets and DEG-based enrichment: if no overlap among the top-10, annotate the cluster as “uncertain” and include a note in cluster_summary to prompt curation. ARI computation: (12) Keep ARI on test as-is but also report test coverage explicitly (already returning n_test_used) and add NMI for complementary assessment; do not use any label-based quantities in selection."} </LM_OUTPUT>

