Here is the feedback we got for generated code for data_preprocess.py in the conversation:

<FEEDBACK>- Enforce a strong HVG quota independent of prior coverage. With nearly all genes “prior-covered” (n_prior_covered_genes ≈ 26k), your current selection is dominated by prior degree. Reserve at least 50–60% of MODEL_GENE_CAP for the top train-derived HVGs (including both prior and non-prior HVGs), then fill remaining capacity with the prior-coverage/round‑robin logic. This preserves discriminative variance and improves cluster separability.
- Fix HVG ranking order. np.lexsort uses the last key as primary; your current order makes prior wdegree the primary sort. Make HVG status the primary criterion (put −rank_hvg last), then mean expression, then nbatches, and only then wdegree. This re-centers feature selection on variability rather than prior ubiquity.
- Compute HVGs on train log1p CPM as specified. Right now HVGs are computed pre-normalization; for seurat_v3, run normalize_total/log1p on the train subset used for HVG detection (or pass a pre-normalized/log1p layer) so the variance model isn’t confounded by library size.
- Use batch_key='dataset' for HVG (take union across datasets) to match the plan and ensure batch-robust HVGs. Avoid folding protocol into the HVG batch key unless justified; keep protocol for stratification only.
- Align the split stratification to dataset||protocol (drop domain). This matches the task spec, avoids over-partitioning, and yields more faithful batch composition in train/val/test.
- Do not mutate PRIOR_DIR artifacts. Stop overwriting prior_set_weights.json; write filtered weights only to OUT_SET_WEIGHTS_FILTERED and reference that path in preprocess_metadata.artifacts. Mutating priors across runs can silently desynchronize training and hurt reproducibility/selection stability.
- Make per-set coverage adaptive. When enforcing MIN_PER_SET_COVERAGE, cap by the post-intersection set size (min(MIN_PER_SET_COVERAGE, set_size_after)) to avoid wasting capacity on small sets and free more slots for HVGs.
- Sanity-check detection filter interaction with HVG quota. If many top HVGs fail the 0.5% detection filter in low-depth batches, allow a small overflow buffer (e.g., +5–10% temporary HVG candidates before enforcing the cap) so final selection still meets the HVG quota after exclusions.</FEEDBACK>

